  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: krb5 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "description": "Multiple security vulnerabilities have been identified and fixed in the Kerberos (krb5) network authentication system used in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10. These include unauthenticated memory exhaustion and CPU denial-of-service (DoS) attacks, memory leaks, null pointer dereferences causing DoS, improper authorization, unauthorized key resets, and request alteration leading to information disclosure. The update also includes various bug fixes and enhancements to improve stability and security.",
